<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4537"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 10:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Of interest I find that the nursery rhyme &#34;Curly Locks&#34; mentions swine and in his first puzzle he has pig twice along with the word sow. <BR> <BR>The words I find most curious are: <BR> <BR>PJ <BR>elm <BR>steam <BR>leo <BR>sos <BR>help <BR>boa <BR>toy <BR>dress <BR>poe <BR>sis <BR>amy <BR>nam <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
