<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4545"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 1:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jrl...if any of the information given to police as his bio is to be believed, look in front of the word steam in the puzzle.  There is an N. <BR>Nsteam is a type of train and in his bio he talks of life long interest in trains.  So I think the word is nsteam not just steam.  Google &#34;nsteam wichita&#34; and see what you get.  It will suprise you!!!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
