<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10561"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 10:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I must say that I&#39;m impressed with everyone&#39;s work.  I only found 54 words/number groupings &#40;although I consider most of the 2 and 3 letter words I found somewhat iffy, since it&#39;s easier to form such words with randomly chosen letters&#41;.  In addition to DRADRE &#40;an obvious anagram of D RADER, near his address, 6220&#41;, I also found FOX and, believe it or not, TOM.  Thing is, much like the D RADER anagram, the FOX and TOM letter groupings are not found in straight lines like all the other words: in block 1 of the symbols, line 2, 2nd from right is F, then up to line 1, 3rd from right to O, then down one to X.  For Tom, look down to block 3, line 1 5th from left for T.  Go down to line 2, 4th from left for O, then down to line 3 and back to 5th from left for M. <BR> <BR>I would normally be inclined to disregard these as artifacts coincidental to the puzzle, except for the fact that D RADER occurs in a similar fashion in block 2, as does his address &#40;well, street number anyway&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10561-->
<!--Post: 10572--><!--Time: 1110014881-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10572"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 1:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed, just below RADER - forming a part of it in fact, we find OFFICER to get &#34;Officer Rader,&#34; his title when catching dogs.  These guys always feel compelled to &#34;sign&#34; their work.  And like ALA, we have another palindrome!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10572-->
<!--Post: 10672--><!--Time: 1110123897-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10672"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 7:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I´v been looking at the puzzel and this is what I came up with.  <BR>ALL THE WORDS ARE TO BE FOUND IN THE PUZZLE <BR> <BR>MO: <BR> <BR>BUILD FANTASIES <BR>ODD SEX DETAILS <BR> <BR>PROWL <BR>SPOT VICTIM <BR>FOLLOW <BR> <BR>PLAN TEAM <BR>GO FOR IT <BR> <BR>ID: <BR>LARRY ANDERSON <BR>WICHITA TELPHONE CO <BR>SCHOOL OFFICER <BR> <BR>HIT STRONG <BR>FRAP &#40;to draw tight &#40;as with ropes or cables&#41; <BR> <BR>RU: <BR>DR &#40;Dennis Rader&#41; FAKE: <BR> <BR>ADH : NEW/OLD MODEL <BR>LE : MAD PET <BR>REALTOR : SALE <BR>INSURANCE : WE HELP <BR>HANDYMAN: WRONG ADDRESS  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10672-->
<!--Post: 10673--><!--Time: 1110124952-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10673"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In addition: <BR>&#40;316&#41; is the prefix for Wichita and Park City telephone#&#39;s &#40;316&#41; 268-6628 &#40;MNBV&#41;or &#40;316&#41;268-2043 <BR> <BR>USD 259<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10673-->
